Hello. Thank you for using Get Your Drugs Tested. We have analyzed your
sample under the code word --- submission number ---- .



   1. The sample A was tested as a mixture of --- with no evidence of other
   compounds detected above the test detection limit --- . The sample was
   tested negative    *POSITIVE*  for fentanyl or fentanyl analogues by
   test strips, was tested negative    *POSITIVE* for benzodiazepines by
   test strips, was tested negative    *POSITIVE *for medetomidine by test
   strips.
   2. The sample B was tested as a mixture of --- with no evidence of other
   compounds detected above the test detection limit --- . The sample was
   tested negative    *POSITIVE*  for fentanyl or fentanyl analogues by
   test strips, was tested negative    *POSITIVE* for benzodiazepines by
   test strips, was tested negative    *POSITIVE *for medetomidine by test
   strips.





You also can find the test results on the webpage:
https://getyourdrugstested.com/test-results-archive/

There are important disclaimers and limitations to these results which you
should be aware of. Please read all of the following information carefully:

5% DETECTION LIMIT AND ESTIMATED PERCENTAGES

Due to new research on the FTIR spectrometer's limitations and an
unpredictable drug supply, we are not always able to provide exact
percentages for all ingredients in our results. We try to estimate active
ingredients when possible, but due to the FTIR's limitations it can be
difficult to offer accurate percentages, especially with complex mixtures.

The spectrometer has a detection threshold of 5%, so there could be
unidentified ingredients that could change the overall percentages of
identified ones. We also use test strips for fentanyl, benzodiazepines, and
LSD, as they can detect substances in trace amounts. Our percentage
estimates are just general guidelines and not to be used for determining
exact concentration of each component due to these limitations. Our
percentages are only for the visible ingredients seen by the FTIR
spectrometer.

SAMPLE LIMITATIONS
The sample we are testing may not be representative of the entire batch.
For example, when we analyze a portion of a pill, that doesn't mean the
rest of the pill or other pills in the same batch will be consistent with
what was analyzed. A product which is not consistent or evenly mixed may
produce different test results depending on which portion is analyzed.

The best result FTIR can provide for solid samples: if the adulterants are
present in the detection limit, we could detect it. For liquid samples
(oils, water solutions, etc.), and for coated tablets the results are less
useful because water, oils, or tablets' fillings and coatings mask target
compounds' signals.

TEST STRIPS
The fentanyl and benzodiazepine test strips indicate a positive when a
threshold is reached. The fentanyl test strips' threshold is 20 ng/mL, the
benzodiazepine test strips' threshold is 300 ng/mL, the medetomidine test
strips' threshold is 1000 ng/mL, and the LSD test strips' threshold is 50
ng/L. Test strips cannot determine the concentration of a substance. Test
strips cannot differentiate between analogs of different strengths (like
fentanyl vs carfentanil). This means two or more analogs could be present
in the same sample.

SAFER USE
Before taking any drug, it helps to read up on its effects, dose and
timeline. You should avoid using substances alone. Start with a small dose
and go from there. Never share tools, and use new tools each time.

SNORTING SAFETY
If you plan on snorting your drugs, sterilize each surface that will come
into contact with the substance. Try not to use rolled up bills - use fresh
straws or rolled up single use paper. After use, rinse your nasal passages
with sterile water.

INJECTION SAFETY
If you plan on injecting your drugs, use sterile water and an unused
needle.  If you plan on using opioids, consider having naloxone on hand.
Try not to use alone. Stagger use in a group setting. Ideally, always have
naloxone on hand, even if you aren't planning to use opioids.

MIXING SUBSTANCES
Mixing substances generally increases the risks of use. It is recommended
to avoid mixing. If you do plan to use more than one substance, please be
sure to consult TripSit's Guide to Drug Combinations.
https://wiki.tripsit.me/wiki/Drug_combinations

NALOXONE
Come to Get Your Drugs Tested for a one-on-one training. Here are two
videos showing how to use naloxone:
https://vimeo.com/185012011
https://vimeo.com/164669763


GOOD FAITH
All test results are given in good faith. By using this service you agree
to indemnify Get Your Drugs Tested, all employees and directors against any
legal claims regarding harms resulting from the use of any drug or
substance. We take no responsibility for any harms resulting from the use
of any substance which has been analyzed by our service. We do not advocate
or promote the use of any drug. While we strive to provide accurate
results, we do not provide any guarantees regarding the accuracy of our
analysis.


FOR MORE INFORMATION
There are many resources available to help you make informed decisions.
Here are three websites known to have good information:

EROWID: https://www.erowid.org
PSYCHONAUT WIKI: https://psychonautwiki.org
TRIPSIT: https://tripsit.me/


QUESTIONS?
If you have any questions, please don't hesitate to ask us in person, by
phone, or by email.


Thank you for choosing to GYDT,

Best regards, team of GYDT

--0000000000008486a20660d26c0d
